<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-buzzatii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength at 2.908 µm in Drosophila buzzatii (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 88.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 re-ran the script. Analytical lambda is 2.908 µm at 0 Ma. Discrete-mode sweep Pearson r = 0.99995 (RMSE 0.962 µm). Saturated spots sit at 3.53 µm. Ablation growth is negative. KS radial between the card and the pure field is 0.458. Image fitness against the canonical card is 85.4 with CV similarity 84.6 on a 12-frame 720×540 GIF. On a 1.70 mm chord the mode counts are 584 (buzzatii), 19 (bipectinata), and 8 (cyrtoloma). Overall 88.8/100 (faithfulness 88.4, reproducibility 89.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 00782eec; environment: python 3.12, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 85, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 89, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_buzzatii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-buzzatii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 00782eec, image/png, 469642 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 e036de5b2cd1da218273a42f89a3c324d68abbfa376721e0b15a03ad64a715e6 (sha256 e036de5b2cd1da218273a42f89a3c324d68abbfa376721e0b15a03ad64a715e6), spec_fingerprint 08fa3b6fbda37d14034e66aaa32be6a4f2884d2974f79734f2b5414d7f6640c2. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 08fa3b6fbda37d14034e66aaa32be6a4f2884d2974f79734f2b5414d7f6640c2; artifact_sha256: e036de5b2cd1da218273a42f89a3c324d68abbfa376721e0b15a03ad64a715e6; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_buzzatii_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_buzzatii_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=61a3792c4a139711..., datasets/drosophila_buzzatii_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_buzzatii_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=21d216f74bbb2735...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-buzzatii-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite critical wavenumber k_c. | Schnakenberg 1979: activator-inhibitor kinetics with a quadratic autocatalytic term. | Norry, Vilardi & Hasson 1997 and Cortese et al. 2002: wing length and thorax size in D. buzzatii are correlated and respond to selection; inversions rearrange the correlations.; reconstructed_in_script: gamma = 0.518619 so lambda_c = 2.908 µm exactly on this Jacobian. | Fourteen-point gamma sweep: Pearson r = 0.99995, RMSE = 0.962 µm between closed-form and discrete-mode wavelengths. | Saturated field wavelength 3.53 µm (radial FFT), a coarsening residual against the linear target. | Equal diffusion max Re(sigma) = -0.0496. | Species-card segmentation: foreground 0.39-range, coherency about 0.67 versus field coherency about 0.25; KS radial 0.458.; transfer_boundary: The 1.70 mm wing chord is a representative length for mode counting, not a reprinted Norry mean. | Predecessor 85.92 µm and successor 207.6 µm are the registry chronoseries scales, not re-fit here.; does_not_claim: That 2.908 µm was measured by Norry as a pigment spacing. | That the species-card JPEG is a photograph of micro-ocelli. It is the gallery fallback after Commons, iNaturalist, and GBIF returned no CC adult bitmap. | That the modulated card is a pixel copy of a wing SEM.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'KS radial is 0.458 (reference 0). Closed in measure_morphoeval.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Card segmentation reports foreground, circularity, and coherency, each unequal to its reference.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Panel F shows max Re(sigma) for D_v/D_u = 29 and for D_v = D_u.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Saturated wavelength 3.53 µm is reported beside the linear target 2.908 µm (RMSE on the sweep is 0.962 µm).', 'status': 'resolved'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Still one assessor, and the canonical image is a species card rather than a wing micrograph. A second assessor and a CC adult photograph would be the next real gain; neither was available in this run.', 'status': 'open'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.88e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

