<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-buzzatii-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg–Turing wavelength at 2.908 µm in Drosophila buzzatii (Pass 2) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Side by side, the pure field is a spot lattice (micro-ocelli) and the GIF paints that density onto the canonical card, from a blank frame (activator std 0.010) to a spotted frame (std 0.926). The card itself is a radial texture, not a wing micrograph, so the score stays below a photographic match." ;
